# The licensing reason this file used to exist is GONE.
#
# It previously ignored audio outright because every candidate was free-tier
# Suno output, licensed for personal and non-commercial use only, and this
# repository is PUBLIC - pushing one would have been distributing it. The track
# here now is paid-tier Output generated 2026-09-02 and cleared to ship
# (ASSET_LICENCES.md), so MP3s are tracked normally and `git add -f` is no longer
# needed for the bed.
#
# WAV IS STILL IGNORED, for a different reason: masters belong in
# the repo-root audio-masters/, outside the app entirely. Anything in static/ is copied wholesale
# into the build, so a 90 MB WAV here would be handed to every player. If a WAV
# appears in this directory it is in the wrong place, not merely uncommitted.
#
# BEFORE COMMITTING: only ONE track ships, and as it stands only one is here -
# A.mp3, which ACTIVE_TRACK_ID names. The other nine paid-tier takes are benched
# in the repo-root audio-masters/ as MP3s beside their WAV masters. If you copy
# one back in to audition it, MOVE IT BACK OUT before staging: static/ is copied
# wholesale into the build, and git history does not forget - removing a file
# later takes a history rewrite, not a delete commit, and any fork or clone keeps
# its copy. musicTracks.test.ts holds a 9 MB ceiling on this directory and prints
# its total on every run, which is the backstop rather than the rule.
*.wav
*.m4a
*.ogg
*.webm
